{"id": "laguna-honda-federal-fines", "title": "The City’s own nursing hospital: $1.3 million of federal fines since 2019", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.037, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "00a9ac0676a958db", "words": 409, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "span", "ref": ["timeline[0]", "timeline[4]"], "text": "January 2019 to October 2021.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 2.8, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2019-01-04", "to": "2021-10-14", "days": "", "fromLab": "first fine", "toLab": "fifth fine", "kicker": "Laguna Honda Hospital"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 0.72, 1.19, 1.31, 1.81, 2.08]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "span", "ref": ["established[0]", "story[0]", "actors[0]"], "text": "Five federal fines on Laguna Honda Hospital, the City’s own nursing hospital.", "t0": 2.92, "t1": 6.95, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2019-01-04", "to": "2021-10-14", "days": "", "fromLab": "first fine", "toLab": "fifth fine", "kicker": "Laguna Honda Hospital"}, "emph": ["City’s own"], "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.73, 1.05, 1.18, 1.58, 1.85, 2.63, 2.78, 3.08, 3.22, 3.56]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[0]", "links[1]"], "text": "1,230,586 dollars.", "t0": 7.07, "t1": 8.8, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1,230,586", "label": "5 federal fines, 2019 to 2021", "sub": "with denials of federal payment"}, "emph": ["1,230,586"], "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.48, 0.75, 0.94, 1.22]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["status", "established[0]"], "text": "These are the federal Medicare and Medicaid agency’s own records.", "t0": 9.32, "t1": 12.36, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Federal Medicare and Medicaid agency", "kicker": "On the record", "sub": "its own records"}, "emph": ["own records"], "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.35, 0.45, 0.77, 1.24, 1.35, 1.77, 2.32, 2.52]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["status", "innocent[2]"], "text": "Some fines can be reduced on appeal.", "t0": 12.48, "t1": 14.21, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Federal Medicare and Medicaid agency", "kicker": "On the record", "sub": "its own records"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.61, 0.75, 0.89, 1.24, 1.32]}, {"scene": "how", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "links[0]", "actors[1]"], "text": "The City’s health department runs it. Federal inspectors survey it like any nursing home.", "t0": 14.43, "t1": 18.7, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Who pays", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Department of Public Health", "sub": "runs the hospital"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Laguna Honda Hospital", "sub": "the City’s nursing hospital"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Federal inspectors", "sub": "survey, fine, deny payment"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.65, 1.06, 1.35, 1.89, 2.24, 2.81, 3.19, 3.29, 3.47, 3.66, 4.01]}, {"scene": "how", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "The federal file names its owner as the City and County of San Francisco.", "t0": 18.82, "t1": 21.99, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Who pays", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Department of Public Health", "sub": "runs the hospital"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Laguna Honda Hospital", "sub": "the City’s nursing hospital"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Federal inspectors", "sub": "survey, fine, deny payment"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.4, 0.7, 0.93, 1.08, 1.41, 1.57, 1.67, 1.92, 2.04, 2.3, 2.39, 2.56]}, {"scene": "how", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "story[4]"], "text": "So a fine is paid with public money, and a payment denial stops federal money.", "t0": 22.11, "t1": 25.59, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Public money", "kicker": "Who pays", "sub": "a fine is a City cost; a payment denial is federal money not received"}, "emph": ["public money"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.23, 0.45, 0.55, 0.72, 0.85, 1.17, 1.53, 1.71, 1.77, 2.09, 2.55, 2.88, 3.18]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "timeline[1]"], "text": "The first lead: 12 July 2019. How big was the fine?", "t0": 25.81, "t1": 29.86, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "12 July 2019", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "a federal fine"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.38, 0.87, 1.2, 1.63, 1.91, 2.85, 3.03, 3.19, 3.31, 3.4]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "timeline[1]"], "text": "732,999 dollars.", "t0": 29.86, "t1": 32.81, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$732,999", "label": "federal fine, 12 July 2019"}, "emph": ["732,999"], "wt": [0.04, 0.32, 0.63, 1.02, 1.52, 1.72, 2.04, 2.46]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "timeline[1]"], "text": "With it, 27 days of no federal payment for new admissions.", "t0": 33.33, "t1": 36.73, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "27", "label": "days without federal payment for new admissions"}, "emph": ["27 days"], "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.66, 1.26, 1.5, 1.6, 1.77, 2.07, 2.43, 2.57, 2.71]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["timeline[2]"], "text": "That November, another 65,657 dollars, and 39 more days without payment.", "t0": 36.85, "t1": 42.93, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Federal fines, 2019", "rows": [["4 January", "$7,296"], ["12 July", "$732,999"], ["19 November", "$65,657"]]}, "emph": ["65,657"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.92, 1.32, 1.95, 2.41, 2.68, 2.98, 3.59, 4.38, 4.57, 5.02, 5.21, 5.46, 5.74]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["trajectory"], "text": "In 2019 alone: 805,952 dollars of federal fines.", "t0": 43.05, "t1": 48.2, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Federal fines, 2019", "rows": [["4 January", "$7,296"], ["12 July", "$732,999"], ["19 November", "$65,657"]]}, "emph": ["805,952"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.36, 0.68, 1.43, 1.65, 1.94, 2.23, 3.02, 3.27, 3.53, 3.98, 4.3, 4.38, 4.67]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Its inspections recorded 125 citations: 13 at actual harm, 7 at immediate jeopardy.", "t0": 48.32, "t1": 54.5, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Inspections under the first federal number", "rows": [["Citations", "125"], ["At the level of actual harm", "13", 1], ["At immediate jeopardy", "7", 1]]}, "emph": ["immediate jeopardy"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.77, 1.21, 1.4, 1.65, 2.17, 3.31, 3.78, 3.88, 4.21, 4.95, 5.28, 5.37, 5.74]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "timeline[4]"], "text": "The second lead. On 14 October 2021, another fine.", "t0": 54.72, "t1": 58.52, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "14 October 2021", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "another federal fine"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.39, 1.03, 1.23, 1.61, 2.08, 2.35, 3.14, 3.48]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "timeline[4]"], "text": "407,770 dollars, and 90 days of no federal payment.", "t0": 58.64, "t1": 63.47, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$407,770", "label": "federal fine, 14 October 2021", "sub": "90 days without federal payment for new admissions"}, "emph": ["407,770"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.55, 0.86, 1.38, 1.64, 1.88, 2.2, 2.95, 3.17, 3.49, 3.82, 3.96, 4.17, 4.49]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "A second large fine two years on is the federal record of problems not put right.", "t0": 63.59, "t1": 67.44, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the federal record of problems that were not put right"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.43, 0.72, 1.1, 1.31, 1.54, 1.75, 1.85, 1.97, 2.36, 2.7, 2.81, 3.24, 3.42, 3.6]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead. Look the hospital up in the federal tool today.", "t0": 67.66, "t1": 70.68, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The current federal file", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "shows only the last three years"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.4, 1.15, 1.38, 1.49, 1.9, 2.02, 2.08, 2.17, 2.46, 2.7]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "None of those older fines appears. It shows only the last three years.", "t0": 70.8, "t1": 74.38, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The current federal file", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "shows only the last three years"}, "emph": ["None"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.31, 0.54, 0.85, 1.15, 1.98, 2.12, 2.33, 2.51, 2.61, 2.84, 3.07]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "story[1]"], "text": "The 1,230,586 dollars", "t0": 74.5, "t1": 76.08, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "kicker": "Archived federal editions", "text": "All $1,230,586 of the older fines are dated before October 2023 and are missing from the current federal file.", "mark": "$1,230,586"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.37, 0.58, 0.84, 1.03, 1.29]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "story[1]"], "text": "turns up only in the yearly editions since December 2019.", "t0": 76.08, "t1": 79.22, "shot": "b13x", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "kicker": "Archived federal editions", "text": "All $1,230,586 of the older fines are dated before October 2023 and are missing from the current federal file.", "mark": "$1,230,586"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.3, 0.47, 0.73, 0.82, 0.92, 1.2, 1.67, 1.94, 2.35, 2.6]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[0]", "links[2]"], "text": "The fourth lead: the fines went on, under a second federal number.", "t0": 79.44, "t1": 82.73, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Federal fines, $1,286,085 in all", "a": ["first federal number, 2019 to 2021", "5 fines, $1,230,586"], "b": ["second number, 2023 to 2025", "8 fines, $55,499"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.37, 1.11, 1.24, 1.51, 1.68, 2.09, 2.3, 2.37, 2.64, 2.92]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "timeline[5]", "timeline[6]"], "text": "8 more from November 2023 to August 2025: 55,499 dollars.", "t0": 82.85, "t1": 89.67, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Federal fines, $1,286,085 in all", "a": ["first federal number, 2019 to 2021", "5 fines, $1,230,586"], "b": ["second number, 2023 to 2025", "8 fines, $55,499"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["55,499"], "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.57, 0.76, 1.25, 1.53, 2.44, 2.62, 2.92, 3.15, 4.32, 4.83, 5.29, 5.52, 5.8, 6.29]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Inspections under the new number: 39 citations, 6 of them at harm level.", "t0": 89.79, "t1": 94.15, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Inspections under the second federal number", "rows": [["Citations", "39"], ["At harm level", "6", 1]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.77, 0.88, 1.02, 1.76, 2.29, 3.13, 3.39, 3.48, 3.65, 3.79, 4.0]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["notEstablished[3]", "story[2]"], "text": "The files don’t say why the number changed.", "t0": 94.27, "t1": 96.02, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "A second federal number", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "the files show the change, not the reason"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.38, 0.58, 0.73, 0.89, 0.99, 1.24]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[1]", "links[3]"], "text": "The State health department adds 22 enforcement actions since 2021,", "t0": 96.14, "t1": 100.35, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "22", "label": "State enforcement actions since 2021", "sub": "final amounts $538,700; no balance due; 13 still open"}, "emph": ["22"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.35, 0.56, 0.95, 1.18, 1.66, 2.13, 2.87, 3.12, 3.38]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[1]", "links[3]"], "text": "with final amounts of 538,700 dollars, and no balance due.", "t0": 100.35, "t1": 104.45, "shot": "b17x", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "22", "label": "State enforcement actions since 2021", "sub": "final amounts $538,700; no balance due; 13 still open"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.49, 0.77, 0.86, 1.09, 1.35, 1.73, 2.13, 2.38, 2.59, 3.23, 3.41, 3.54, 3.87]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "timeline[7]"], "text": "13 are still open. 6 came after June 2024.", "t0": 104.57, "t1": 108.0, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "22", "label": "State enforcement actions since 2021", "sub": "final amounts $538,700; no balance due; 13 still open"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.55, 0.8, 1.52, 1.86, 2.05, 2.31, 2.56, 2.81]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The records don’t show what each fine was for, or what was paid after appeals.", "t0": 108.22, "t1": 111.56, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["What each fine was for", "How much was paid after appeals, and from which budget", "What the payment denials cost"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.38, 0.59, 0.75, 0.89, 1.05, 1.24, 1.37, 1.87, 2.08, 2.22, 2.34, 2.55, 2.77]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Or what the payment denials cost the hospital.", "t0": 111.68, "t1": 113.88, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["What each fine was for", "How much was paid after appeals, and from which budget", "What the payment denials cost"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.48, 0.58, 0.9, 1.33, 1.59, 1.7]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["innocent[1]"], "text": "A public hospital takes residents other homes turn away, which can mean more complaint surveys.", "t0": 114.0, "t1": 119.01, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A public hospital takes residents other homes turn away."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.43, 0.88, 1.11, 1.55, 1.83, 2.1, 2.3, 3.05, 3.29, 3.45, 3.7, 3.92, 4.36]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The federal survey reports, and the City budget lines that paid the fines.", "t0": 119.13, "t1": 123.65, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The federal survey reports behind each fine"}, {"who": "", "what": "The City budget lines that paid them, after appeal"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.3, 0.6, 1.16, 1.31, 1.61, 1.93, 2.45, 2.59, 2.69, 2.94, 3.27, 3.53, 3.67, 3.85, 3.94]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "The fines are official records. How much the City finally paid is not on file.", "t0": 123.77, "t1": 127.2, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.36, 0.46, 0.81, 1.3, 1.48, 1.66, 1.76, 2.01, 2.33, 2.66, 2.78, 2.95, 3.06]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.32, "t1": 129.38, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.62, 0.77, 1.03, 1.13, 1.22, 1.45, 1.7]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Five fines", "how": "Who pays", "lead1": "July 2019", "lead2": "October 2021", "lead3": "Not in today’s file", "lead4": "It went on", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "timeline"}